#: src/moodlog:4793
msgid "Medication: a Medication button on each day opens the list of that day's doses, each with a pill in the colour of its status, the time, the amount and Taken or Skipped."
msgstr ""

#: src/moodlog:4796
msgid "Medication from Apple Health: with Moodlog for iPhone 1.6, the medications you log in the Health app and the doses you took or skipped arrive with the health data. They show on each day, and the report for your doctor has a Medication section."
msgstr ""

#: src/moodlog:4799
msgid "A daily reminder (☰ → Reminder and kind word): one quiet desktop notification at the time you choose, only on days you haven't logged a mood yet."
msgstr ""

#: src/moodlog:4800
msgid "A kind word on hard days: after a few very hard days close together, the Log shows a short, kind note with a helpline. It never tells anyone, and you can hide it or turn it off."
msgstr ""

#: src/moodlog:4803
msgid "Moodlog for Android 1.1.0 is out: a new look like the iPhone app, a taller calendar, and it finds this PC more reliably when pop-os.local doesn't work on the phone. Nothing changes on the PC."
msgstr ""

#: src/moodlog:4806
msgid "Moodlog for Android: a new app for Android phones that syncs moods, energy, anxiety, notes, events and dreams with this PC, encrypted, and sends sleep, steps and resting heart rate from Health Connect. Phone sync has the steps to set it up."
msgstr ""

#: src/moodlog:4811
msgid "A privacy policy: ☰ menu → Privacy shows in short what Moodlog does with your data (nothing leaves your devices except the encrypted phone sync), with a link to the full policy."
msgstr ""

#: src/moodlog:4814
msgid "The phone sync receiver no longer writes the address of a request to the system log in full, so a token sent in the address can't end up there."
msgstr ""

#: src/moodlog:4818
msgid "Encrypted phone sync: Moodlog for iPhone 1.4 encrypts everything it sends with your token, and the token itself never crosses the network. Phone sync shows whether the last connection was encrypted, and has a new Change token button."
msgstr ""

#: src/moodlog:4823
msgid "A welcome tour for new users: a few friendly, animated steps that point at each part of the window and explain it. It opens by itself on a new install; see it any time from the ☰ menu → Show the tour."
msgstr ""

#: src/moodlog:4828
msgid "Doctor report: “Also what the dreams were about” can always be ticked, and ticking it includes dreams too. Before, it stayed greyed out until “Include dreams” was ticked, so it was easy to miss."
msgstr ""

#: src/moodlog:4833
msgid "After an update, the phone sync receiver switches to the new version by itself. Before, it kept running the old one until it was restarted, so new things such as dreams did not sync."
msgstr ""

#: src/moodlog:4838
msgid "Dream journal: a new Dreams tab. Write down a dream with how it felt and tags such as nightmare or vivid, or note that you didn't remember one. Dreams show as a moon in the calendar, with a summary in the tab and in Charts, and sync with the iPhone."
msgstr ""

#: src/moodlog:4841
msgid "The doctor report can include dreams: off by default, then just how many and the nightmare nights, or also what they were about."
msgstr ""

#: src/moodlog:4843
msgid "Tabs take less room, so the window fits in half a screen again."
msgstr ""

#: src/moodlog:4846
msgid "Moodlog speaks Italian. It follows your system language, or choose one in the ☰ menu → Language. Dates, charts, the doctor report and exports are translated too."
msgstr ""

#: src/moodlog:4850
msgid "A “What's new” window opens once after each update, with the full changelog. Open it again any time from the ☰ menu."
msgstr ""

#: src/moodlog:4854
msgid "Tahoe style: the selected Energy and Anxiety numbers were invisible (white on white). They are blue again, in light and dark."
msgstr ""

#: src/moodlog:4856
msgid "Screenshots of the app are now in the README."
msgstr ""

#: src/moodlog:4859
msgid "Moodlog for iPhone: a new app that syncs moods, energy, anxiety, notes and events with Moodlog on your PC over your home Wi-Fi."
msgstr ""

#: src/moodlog:4861
msgid "Every entry and event now has an ID and a change time: the newest change wins, deletions sync too, and nothing is overwritten when two devices save at once."
msgstr ""

#: src/moodlog:4863
msgid "Saving merges changes written meanwhile by the phone or another computer."
msgstr ""

#: src/moodlog:4864
msgid "Your existing data is upgraded automatically."
msgstr ""

